   "reasoning_content": "Let me analyze this bug report. The issue is about encrypting PDF files - when the same PDF is encrypted again, it overwrites the previously encrypted file instead of creating a new file with a unique name.\n\nExpected behavior: When encrypting a PDF that already has an encrypted version, a new file should be created with a unique identifier (like `abc_encrypted_123.pdf`) rather than overwriting `abc_encrypted.pdf`.\n\nLet me first explore the codebase to understand its structure and find where PDF encryption happens.\n",
   "tool_calls": [
    {
     "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a78fa7213b44f64e",
     "function_name": "agent",
     "arguments": {
      "description": "Explore PDF encryption code",
      "prompt": "I need to find the code responsible for PDF encryption/password protection in this Android project. \n\nThe bug is about encrypted PDF files being overwritten when the same PDF is encrypted again. Specifically:\n1. When you encrypt a PDF (e.g., abc.pdf), it creates abc_encrypted.pdf\n2. If you encrypt abc.pdf again with a new password, it overwrites the existing abc_encrypted.pdf instead of creating a uniquely named file\n\nSearch for:\n- Files related to PDF encryption, password protection, or file encryption\n- Code that creates files with \"_encrypted\" suffix\n- Any file naming logic related to encrypted PDFs\n- Look for patterns like \"encrypted\", \"pdf\", \"password\", \"EncryptPdf\" in the codebase\n\nBe very thorough - check all Java, Kotlin, and XML files. Look at the app/ directory structure carefully.",
      "subagent_type": "Explore"
     }
    }
